# {{.Name}} ({{.Type}})

{{ .Description | trimspace }}

For product context, see [Service accounts](https://ona.com/docs/ona/organizations/service-accounts), [Configuring repository access](https://ona.com/docs/ona/runners/configuring-repository-access), and [Git providers](https://ona.com/docs/ona/source-control/overview).

**Prerequisite:** The target service account must be authorized for the selected runner before Terraform creates the Git authentication. The example adds the service account to a group, grants that group the `user` role on the same runner with `ona_runner_role_assignment`, and makes the Git authentication depend on both resources. The `user` role is sufficient. Permissions held only by the provider credential are insufficient because host-authentication lifecycle requests run as the target service account.

